IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ssa-payments`

-- Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), ss 7(5), 23(5A)-(5D), 43, 44, 94, 103, 540-543B, 593, 598, 954, 957A, 1061ZG, 1064, 1067G, 1071 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_social-security-act-1991.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- ILLUSTRATIVE INPUTS. The Act does not state the maximum payment rates, assets value limits, income free areas or income limits in
-- force on the scenario dates (all are indexed), and the deposit has LOST the reduction formulas of point 1064-E10 and Table G-2. Every
-- such figure below is an illustrative input chosen by the encoder, not a figure read in the deposit: maximum payment rates of $20,000
-- a year (single) and $15,000 (each member of a couple), the Table G-1 and E-1 base figures used as if they were the limits in force,
-- and reduction rates of 50c (single) and 25c (each member of a couple) per dollar of income excess and 7.8c (single) and 3.9c (each
-- member of a couple) per dollar of assets excess. The scenarios give NO asset or income figures for any of the lives; the asset values
-- below are invented to show the shape of the refusal the scenarios record. The cases test the encoding, not the lives' outcomes.

